# Sensitive paths for shipping-work-python-fastapi's doc-check.sh (Step 1.5).
# One path per line; blank lines and #-comments ignored. Entries match whole
# path SEGMENTS at any depth. This file REPLACES the script's built-in
# defaults wholesale — it does not extend them (#75, gregoryfoster/skills#252).
#
# Dropped from the defaults because nothing in this tree can match them:
# CHANGELOG.md, schema.sql, alembic/versions/, src/models/, .env.example.
# Replicator has no DB and no changelog, and both env files live outside the
# repo or are git-ignored (see docs/ENVIRONMENT.md).

# Agent- and human-facing entry points. AGENTS.md inventories the rest.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md

# Dependency surface: the co-core pin and the wheelhouse story are documented
# prose, not just lockfile state (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
pyproject.toml
uv.lock

# Module layout. Whole tree, not the per-package list the defaults used: a NEW
# top-level package under src/ is exactly the change that leaves AGENTS.md's
# Project Layout stale, and a per-package list would miss it.
src/

# Runnable surface — docs/COMMANDS.md lists every script with its flags.
scripts/

# The systemd unit and its guards (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, Server Lifecycle).
deploy/

# CI gates, including the charter enforcement in tests/test_boundaries.py.
.github/workflows/

# Normative contracts — linked from sibling repos, so drift here is cross-repo.
docs/contracts/

# Skill inventory, mirrored in two places and inventoried by docs/SKILLS.md.
# skills-vendor/ is deliberately absent: the daily auto-refresh bumps that
# pointer without any doc consequence.
skills/
.claude/skills/
.claude/hooks/

# The SocratiCode manifest is a source, not the artifact — editing it without
# re-indexing leaves the highest-authority answer stale (docs/SOCRATICODE.md).
.socraticodecontextartifacts.json
